  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Hokm (Iranian Trick-taking). Players: 4, 2 partnerships (fixed_cross). Deck: Standard 52. Direction: anticlockwise. Hâkem selection: deal until Ace. Deal: 5 cards → Hâkem declares trump → 8 more (13 total). Play: Hâkem leads trick 1. Must follow suit. Highest trump wins; else highest of led suit. Winner leads next. Hand: first team to 7 tricks wins (1pt, slam 7-0=2pt, Kot 13-0=3pt). Hâkem stays if team wins, else rotates right. Match: first to 7 points.',
    Player: "Hokm: 4 players, 2 partnerships (partners sit opposite). Deal cards face-up until someone gets an Ace — they're the Hâkem (Ruler). Dealer (to Hâkem's right) deals 5 cards each. Hâkem declares the trump suit. Then 8 more cards dealt (13 total). Hâkem leads first trick. Play anticlockwise. Must follow suit. Highest trump wins; else highest of led suit. First team to 7 tricks wins the hand (1 point; 7-0 slam = 2 points). First team to 7 match points wins!",
    objective: 'Win tricks as a partnership. First team to win 7 tricks in a hand scores points. First team to accumulate 7 match points wins.',
    gameplay: "1. HÂKEM SELECTION: Deal cards face-up anticlockwise until someone gets an Ace — they are the Hâkem (Ruler).\n2. DEALING: Player to Hâkem's right deals 5 cards to each player anticlockwise.\n3. TRUMP DECLARATION: Hâkem looks at 5 cards and declares the trump suit (Hokm). Hâkem must not show cards to anyone.\n4. REMAINING DEAL: Dealer deals remaining 8 cards to each player (13 total per player).\n5. TRICK PLAY: Hâkem leads the first trick. Play proceeds anticlockwise. Each player plays one card.\n6. FOLLOWING SUIT: Must follow the suit led if possible. If void, may play any card including trump.\n7. TRICK WINNER: Highest trump wins. If no trump played, highest card of the led suit wins. Winner leads next trick.\n8. HAND SCORING: Team that wins 7+ out of 13 tricks wins the hand. Score: 1 point normally, 2 points for a slam (7-0). Some play Kot (all 13 tricks) = 3 points.\n9. HÂKEM ROTATION: If Hâkem's team wins, Hâkem stays. If they lose, the player to Hâkem's right becomes the new Hâkem.\n10. MATCH END: First team to 7 match points wins.",
    keyRules: [
      'Must follow suit if possible. If void in the led suit, any card may be played including trump.',
      'Hâkem declares trump after seeing only their first 5 cards.',
      'Highest trump wins the trick. If no trump, highest card of led suit wins.',
      'Trick winner leads the next trick. Play is anticlockwise.',
      'First team to win 7 tricks takes the hand (1 point). 7-0 sweep = 2 points (slam).',
      'Hâkem stays if their team wins; otherwise rotates to the right.',
      'Match is first team to 7 match points.',
    ],
