    turnFlow: "1. HÂKEM SELECTION: Deal cards face-up anticlockwise until someone gets an Ace — they are the Hâkem (Ruler).\n2. DEALING: Player to Hâkem's right deals 5 cards to each player anticlockwise.\n3. TRUMP DECLARATION: Hâkem looks at 5 cards and declares the trump suit (Hokm). Hâkem must not show cards to anyone.\n4. REMAINING DEAL: Dealer deals remaining 8 cards to each player (13 total per player).\n5. TRICK PLAY: Hâkem leads the first trick. Play proceeds anticlockwise. Each player plays one card.\n6. FOLLOWING SUIT: Must follow the suit led if possible. If void, may play any card including trump.\n7. TRICK WINNER: Highest trump wins. If no trump played, highest card of the led suit wins. Winner leads next trick.\n8. HAND SCORING: Team that wins 7+ out of 13 tricks wins the hand. Score: 1 point normally, 2 points for a slam (7-0). Some play Kot (all 13 tricks) = 3 points.\n9. HÂKEM ROTATION: If Hâkem's team wins, Hâkem stays. If they lose, the player to Hâkem's right becomes the new Hâkem.\n10. MATCH END: First team to 7 match points wins.",
